course: dictionary
lesson: 3804
title: One word, two homes
level: primary-4
stars: 1
explain: Some words have more than one meaning. The words around them, the context, tell you which meaning the writer wants. «The forecourt has a garden-seat, a roller, ferns in wire baskets, and plaster statues.» Seats, ferns and statues belong outside a building, so here a forecourt is the open area in front of a building.
explain: A forecourt can also be part of a sports court. In tennis, the forecourt is the part nearest the net. If a sentence talks about players, a ball or a net, that is your clue.
explain: Use the swap check. Put each meaning into the sentence and see which one fits. «The forecourt had ferns in wire baskets» makes sense with the open-area meaning. Try the tennis meaning there and it makes no sense.
fact: A forecourt is an open area in front of a building.
fact: A petrol station forecourt is where the petrol pumps are.
fact: Safety rules on a petrol station forecourt say no smoking and no phones.
fact: In tennis, the forecourt is the part of the court nearest the net.
fact: Players step into the forecourt to hit volleys.
exercise: «The forecourt has ferns in wire baskets and plaster statues.» What is a forecourt in this sentence? | A type of statue | *An open area in front of a building | A kind of plant | A part of a tennis court
exercise: Maya sees a sign at the petrol station: «No smoking on the forecourt.» Where is the forecourt? | On the tennis net | *In front of the building, where the petrol pumps are | At the top of a hill | Inside the car
exercise: Sam steps forward and hits a quick volley. Which forecourt is he in? | *The part of the court nearest the net | Under the garden seat | The back line of the court | The garden in front of the house
test: «The forecourt was full of ferns and a garden seat.» What does forecourt mean? | A tall fence | *An open area in front of a building | The part of a tennis court nearest the net | A dark cupboard
test: Which sentence uses forecourt to mean the part of a tennis court? | Dad parked the car on the forecourt | The forecourt had ferns in wire baskets | The petrol pumps stood in the forecourt | *Ella ran into the forecourt to hit a volley over the net
exam: Jayden reads «The forecourt has a garden-seat and a roller» and then hears about tennis. What should he do to find the meaning? | Guess at random | Skip the word for ever | *Read the words around it and try each meaning in the sentence | Look only at the first letter
